WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:06.720
Dr. Anderson Montgomery, a researcher for
the SCP Foundation, was 35 years old when

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.370
he received the call he knew would change
his life forever.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:14.580
He was one of those guys you could best describe
as married to the job.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:18.070
He’d never shown any interest in outside
hobbies.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:23.539
As far as anyone at the Foundation knew, he’d
never developed a love life or had any real

00:00:23.539 --> 00:00:26.320
enthusiasm toward the idea of one.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:32.320
He’d devoted all his time and energy to
work: Grinding away, putting in the hours,

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.510
and doing whatever his employers asked of
him.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.890
And now, he was going to be punished for it.

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:46.170
The call came from a Senior Site-19 Researcher
Dr. Gregory Vandivier, an old, stern Foundation

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:49.580
veteran he’d worked under on a few projects
in the past.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:55.100
Dr. Vandivier, with his trademark calm, authoritative
voice, said, “You’ve been selected for

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.360
SCP-231 duty.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:00.050
You’ll be working directly under my supervision.

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:05.059
Pending the results of the mandated psychological
evaluations, you’ll be assisting me and

00:01:05.059 --> 00:01:09.840
the rest of the SCP-231 team in carrying out
Procedure 110 Montauk.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.280
I look forward to working with you.”

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.289
The feeling was not mutual.

00:01:14.289 --> 00:01:19.840
When the call ended, the normally stoic and
professional Dr. Montgomery was in a cold

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:20.840
sweat.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:25.530
He’d heard legends about SCP-231 and of
Procedure 110 Montauk.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:30.290
The Foundation has needed to do some extreme
things to keep dangerous anomalies contained

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:38.590
- from sacrificing people to SCP-2845, The
Deer, and SCP-974, the Treehouse Predator,

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:44.860
to murdering any civilian who gets too close
to SCP-823, the Carnival of Horrors.

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:48.310
But Procedure 110 Montauk is a different league.

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:53.759
It’s a containment measure so horrifying
that for many at the Foundation, it’s literally

00:01:53.759 --> 00:01:55.689
unspeakable.

00:01:55.689 --> 00:02:00.090
The knowledge of his impending transfer drove
Dr. Montgomery to do something he’d never

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:02.100
done before: Socialize.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:07.819
He asked around to some of his fellow Site-19
researchers, querying as to whether any of

00:02:07.819 --> 00:02:15.680
them had performed - or knew anyone who had
performed - Procedure 110 Montauk on SCP-231.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:21.370
He was met with many blank, haunted faces,
and stares that seemed to look right through

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:22.370
him.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:27.310
They told him that nobody in the history of
the Foundation had ever taken on Montauk detail

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:31.210
and not accepted a course of amnestic therapy
afterward.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:34.950
Nobody who’d done it wanted to remember
their part in the atrocity.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:39.580
And perhaps that was the only consolation:
Once you’ve done it, at least they’ll

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:42.209
give you the choice to forget.

00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:47.330
As Dr. Vandivier had alluded to over the phone,
the battery of tests performed to prepare

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:50.980
Dr. Montgomery for his new duty was extensive.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:55.520
He was given the Milgram Obedience Examination
- which involved being ordered to knowingly

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:58.290
give an innocent man electrical shocks.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:03.590
You have to score at least 72 on the test
to qualify for SCP-231 detail.

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:07.769
Thorough background checks were conducted
into every facet of his life.

00:03:07.769 --> 00:03:12.470
No stone was unturned in making sure that
Dr. Montgomery would be the right man for

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:13.569
the job.

00:03:13.569 --> 00:03:19.280
And nobody was less certain about the answer
to that than Dr. Anderson Montgomery himself.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:22.790
He knew about SCP-231.

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:24.630
Everyone at the Foundation did.

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:30.160
After all, if there was a 100-megaton nuclear
bomb sitting in your bedroom closet, wouldn’t

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:32.980
you at least want to know that it was there?

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:38.270
That was what SCP-231 was all about - except
that it makes a nuclear weapon look like a

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:41.150
gentle kiss goodnight in comparison.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:47.900
If ever SCP-231 is compromised, it means the
end of reality as we know it and the beginning

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:49.170
of a true nightmare.

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:53.349
It’d all started with a warehouse a long
time ago.

00:03:53.349 --> 00:03:57.749
A warehouse purchased and registered under
the name, “D. Spivak”, believed to be

00:03:57.749 --> 00:04:03.730
the infamous Person of Interest Dipesh Spivak,
a power player in a little cult known as The

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:06.470
Children of the Scarlet King.

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:11.730
As the name suggests, they worship the eponymous
Scarlet King, one of the most powerful and

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:18.289
dangerous beings in the entire multiverse
- a Nightmare God who represents chaos, cruelty,

00:04:18.289 --> 00:04:19.860
and primal violence.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:24.009
The Scarlet King’s followers were constantly
planning and executing new attempts to allow

00:04:24.009 --> 00:04:29.400
their master into our reality, and the latest
one was centered around this humble little

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:34.620
warehouse on the edge of a city perhaps not
too far from yours...

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:39.759
Noise complaints had caused suspicion to fall
upon this warehouse - screaming and chanting

00:04:39.759 --> 00:04:41.500
in the dead of night.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.570
Loud footsteps.

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:44.860
Scraping metal.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:48.780
When the police arrived to check in on the
noise complaint, they were met with startling

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:49.780
force.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:53.770
Robed strangers with heavy weaponry, gunning
them down left and right.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:56.170
What on earth were these maniacs defending
in there?

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:57.280
A drug lab?

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.500
Arms dealing?

00:04:58.500 --> 00:04:59.530
Human trafficking?

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:02.330
The true answer would be even worse.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:07.570
Luckily for the first responders, they had
an unexpected cavalry swoop in to save the

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:12.910
day: A well-armed and well-trained SCP Foundation
Mobile Task Force.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:17.750
They repelled the cultists and soon took over
the investigation, only to find that the terrible

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:23.110
secret inside the warehouse was going to be
a handful - even for them.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:29.370
Seven girls, chained up and neglected, each
one the victim of horrible rituals and deeds

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:33.720
by the cultists, appeared to be at the late
stages of pregnancy.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:38.680
The Foundation escorted the seven girls away
to a secure containment chamber, apprehending

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:44.080
a few of their captors alive, and also managing
to collect a series of notebooks detailing

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:46.110
the disgusting nature of the rituals.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:52.789
It was a perfect example of how sometimes,
mere humans can be the greatest monsters of

00:05:52.789 --> 00:05:53.789
all.

00:05:53.789 --> 00:05:58.780
Speaking of monsters, something awful happened
the night that the seven girls - designated

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:03.510
SCP-231-1 through 7 - were brought in.

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:09.500
During the recovery operation, SCP-231-1 began
having violent contractions and then suddenly

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:10.830
gave birth.

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:15.681
The incredibly aggressive anomaly she gave
birth to that night killed not only her, but

00:06:15.681 --> 00:06:21.270
over a hundred others - the doctors and researchers
who were unlucky enough to be in the area,

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:25.580
and many of the trained Foundation soldiers
that were sent in to stop it.

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:30.580
It became quickly apparent that this situation
was out of control, and each one of the remaining

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:34.720
six girls might give birth to an even more
powerful threat.

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:40.340
Senior Researcher Dr. Robert Montauk was brought
in to take over the SCP-231 case.

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:44.760
The debate would go on among Foundation staff
for years as to whether he was the best or

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:47.819
worst person for that particular job.

00:06:47.819 --> 00:06:52.819
You see, Dr. Montauk had a storied history
with the Children of the Scarlet King, the

00:06:52.819 --> 00:06:59.750
cult that had created SCP-231: Many years
before, his younger brother, Jacob, had gone

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:05.580
missing, never to be seen again, and he believed
that they were the ones behind the disappearance.

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:09.720
Naturally, Dr. Montauk thought a little revenge
was in order.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:15.569
Many at the Foundation believe that this rage,
this desire to get back at the cultists and

00:07:15.569 --> 00:07:20.520
the Scarlet King, caused him to create a procedure
as horrifying as the one that would forever

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:22.220
bear his name.

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:26.550
He conceived it after obsessively reading
through the cults’ notebooks, and conducting

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:30.560
brutal interrogations against the members
of the cult that they had captured.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:36.490
He had taken the cult’s own inhuman methods
and reverse engineered them, making them even

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:38.730
more barbaric in the process.

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:43.340
It was an act so devoid of compassion and
decency that many believe Dr. Montauk would

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:48.180
later go insane and become an enemy of the
very Foundation that allowed him to exact

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:49.550
his revenge.

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:55.800
Since then, SCP-231 has become an anomaly
marred by tragedy after tragedy.

00:07:55.800 --> 00:08:02.080
Foundation scientists attempted to terminate
the pregnancy of SCP-231-2, but instead, this

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:05.139
simply induced her to give birth.

00:08:05.139 --> 00:08:11.939
It was another huge disaster, with scores
of people - SCP-231-2 included - being killed

00:08:11.939 --> 00:08:13.639
in the process.

00:08:13.639 --> 00:08:19.419
SCP-231-3 is believed to have died due to
the sheer intensity of the Procedure 110 Montauk

00:08:19.419 --> 00:08:24.740
protocols, and once again released an entity
in the process that went on to cause a massive

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:26.659
loss of life.

00:08:26.659 --> 00:08:33.339
SCP-231-4 was given a sample of SCP-500, the
Panacea, which is a collection of pills that

00:08:33.339 --> 00:08:34.760
can cure anything.

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:40.149
It did cause her to successfully eject the
231 fetus, but this fetus then went on to

00:08:40.149 --> 00:08:46.680
cause another mass casualty event, killing
SCP-231-4 and so many others.

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:53.329
A botched application of the Montauk procedure
was what set off SCP-231-5, and resulted in

00:08:53.329 --> 00:08:59.709
not only a huge number of additional deaths
but the destruction of Site 231-Aleph - the

00:08:59.709 --> 00:09:04.149
entire site used in the holding of SCP-231
specimens.

00:09:04.149 --> 00:09:10.670
The Montauk procedure also caused the incident
with SCP-231-6, though in a slightly more

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:12.130
indirect way.

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:17.930
A rogue agent had been driven mad with guilt
by his part in Procedure 110 Montauk and tried

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:19.620
to escape with SCP-231-6.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:27.529
The resulting firefight caused SCP-231-6 to
give birth, killing her, the rogue agent,

00:09:27.529 --> 00:09:30.940
and everyone else unlucky enough to be caught
nearby.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:35.100
Every time one of these incidents occurred,
the disaster got worse.

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:41.310
By all current Foundation projections, if
ever SCP-231-7 gave birth, it’d be a coin

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:45.320
toss on whether it caused an XK-Class End
of the World Scenario.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:51.340
And that’s not the kind of risk the SCP
Foundation can ever leave to chance.

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:58.290
Performing Procedure 110 Montauk at least
once every 24 hours on SCP-231-7 was the only

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:02.970
way to ensure humanity’s continued safety
from the Scarlet King.

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:08.220
The D-Classes forced to perform the procedure
first-hand are even given explosive collars,

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:13.480
so the Foundation can literally blow their
head off if they show a moment’s hesitation.

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:18.600
All these thoughts and so many others were
swimming through Dr. Anderson Montgomery’s

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:24.889
mind when he was finally escorted to the secure
and secretive facility where SCP-231-7 is

00:10:24.889 --> 00:10:29.110
kept and Procedure 110 Montauk is carried
out.

00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:33.700
It’s so classified that Dr. Montgomery needed
to be blindfolded and switched between seven

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:36.110
different vehicles during the journey.

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:41.040
He was told that if ever he attempted to remove
the blindfold in transit, he would be immediately

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:42.040
shot.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:43.180
No questions asked.

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:48.940
When he arrived, he found himself staring
into the stony face of Dr. Gregory Vandivier.

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:53.050
A weathered man who had seen things he wished
he could forget.

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:57.779
When young Dr. Montgomery walked with him,
they walked in relative silence, except for

00:10:57.779 --> 00:11:00.889
when Dr. Vandivier needed to deliver an order.

00:11:00.889 --> 00:11:04.480
You just didn’t talk about the kind of thing
they were about to take part in.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:08.670
Though Dr. Montgomery could feel it looming
over him like a shadow.

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:13.610
They passed through more security checkpoints
on the way to the control room, as Dr. Montgomery’s

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:15.360
palms began to sweat.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:21.089
He wished with everything in him that he could
turn back, that he could run for his life,

00:11:21.089 --> 00:11:22.470
but there was no time.

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:26.240
If he did that now, he’d probably catch
a bullet in the back.

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:28.889
But would even that be better than this?

00:11:28.889 --> 00:11:31.850
The two doctors soon arrived in the control
room.

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:35.240
Monitors everywhere showed an empty room with
a single bed.

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:39.330
Curiously, Dr. Montgomery noticed that a D-Class
was fluffing a pillow on the bed.

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:42.260
That’s when the countdown began.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:45.430
Procedure 110 Montauk was about to commence.

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:49.850
The sheer anticipation had Dr. Montgomery
on the edge of vomiting, and when the doors

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:55.839
opened, and a heavily pregnant SCP-231-7 entered
the chamber, he almost fainted.

00:11:55.839 --> 00:11:57.660
The girl laid out on the bed.

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:00.709
Moments later, a lone D-Class entered the
room.

00:12:00.709 --> 00:12:02.800
He was carrying a book.

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:09.160
He took a seat on a chair near SCP-231-7’s
bed, and said, "Hello again, Katherine.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:12.339
I brought you a new one tonight, it's called
Goodnight Moon.

00:12:12.339 --> 00:12:13.510
Is that okay?"

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:20.720
He then, to the immense surprise of Dr. Montgomery,
read SCP-231-7 a bedtime story until she drifted

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:22.070
off to sleep.

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:25.570
And with that, Procedure 110 Montauk was over.

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:28.269
Dr. Montgomery didn’t understand.

00:12:28.269 --> 00:12:29.709
Had he gone insane?

00:12:29.709 --> 00:12:34.209
Did his mind invent all of this just to be
more comfortable with what he was actually

00:12:34.209 --> 00:12:35.209
seeing?

00:12:35.209 --> 00:12:40.149
But before he could ponder anymore, Dr. Vandivier
placed a fatherly hand on Dr. Montgomery’s

00:12:40.149 --> 00:12:43.279
shoulder, and finally gave him his explanation.

00:12:43.279 --> 00:12:46.150
The piece of the puzzle that made everything
come together.

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:51.270
You see, Procedure 110 Montauk has never been
a monstrous method of torture.

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:54.290
It’s never been a horrific atrocity.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:58.449
But for it to work, everyone needed to believe
it was.

00:12:58.449 --> 00:13:03.180
After all, The Scarlet King doesn’t watch
over everything like some biblical God.

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:10.519
He only feels, and what he feels strongest
of all is terror, hate, and revulsion.

00:13:10.519 --> 00:13:16.800
No harm ever needed to befall Katherine, the
girl known as SCP-231-7, because the worst

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:20.029
thing imaginable had already happened to her.

00:13:20.029 --> 00:13:26.160
The Foundation instead did something far more
clever: Through lying to even their own ranks,

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:28.660
they lied to the Scarlet King, too.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:31.950
It was fear alone that sold the lie.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:35.230
Enough fear to mask the scent of their hidden
compassion.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:41.230
And it was a lie that the Scarlet King himself,
along with the rest of us, bought hook, line,

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:42.560
and sinker.

00:13:42.560 --> 00:13:45.480
After all, evil doesn’t beat evil.

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:46.480
Good does.

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:52.829
Now go check out “SCP-001 - The Scarlet
King” and “Children of SCP-001 The Scarlet

00:13:52.829 --> 00:13:59.040
King - Is SCP-999 Really His Son?” for more
on the Scarlet King and the way his horrific

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:00.769
deeds affect our world!

